            "title": "Why we started Scentspired: life is too short to save your good perfume for best",
            "excerpt": "There is a glass cabinet in quite a lot of British homes. It contains the good china that never gets used, a candle that smells incredible but is too nice to burn, and at least one bottle of designer perfume that gets treated like a controlled substance. You bought it, or someone bought it for you, and now it lives there. Being admired. Not worn. Sprayed approximately twice a year on occasions significant enough to justify it. This is not what it was made for.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/why-we-started-scentspired-life-is-too-short-to-save-your-good-perfume-for-best",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
          }
        },
        "blog_item_iPHRV7": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/The_Best_Perfume_Gift_Guide_jpg.jpg",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "The Best Perfume Gift Guide: luxury inspired perfumes UK sorted by personality not price,for everyone from your mum to your mate",
            "excerpt": "Buying perfume for someone else is, if we are being honest about it, a minor act of\nbravery. You are making a call about how someone smells, which is one of the more\npersonal things a person can have an opinion about. Get it right and you are a\ngenius. Get it wrong and they will smile politely while quietly adding it to the back of\nthe bathroom cabinet, next to the candle they will never burn and a half-used bottle\nof something gifted by their nan at Christmas three years ago.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/the-best-perfume-gift-guide-luxury-inspired-perfumes-uk-sorted-by-personality-not-price-for-everyone-from-your-mum-to-your-mate",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
          }
