        "blog_item_fWQJYB": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Forget_the_Scented_Candle_Thumbnail_jpg.jpg",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "Forget the scented the fragrance gift guide sorted by personality, not price",
            "excerpt": "On far too many special occasions to count, someone unwraps a scented candle,\nsays ahhhh lovely, and quietly adds it to the back of cupboard that already houses\nfour other scented candles nobody has burned. This is not a personal failing. It is\nsimply what happens when gift buying becomes about filling a category rather than\nknowing a person. Socks, biscuits, candles: all perfectly nice, all instantly forgettable,\nall bought under time pressure in the last aisle of a Sainsbury’s shop that was not the\nplan.\nFragrance solves this problem properly, but only if you stop shopping by budget and\nstart shopping by character. A 15 quid bottle chosen because it is unmistakably them\nwill outperform a 60 quid gift set chosen because it was sitting next to the till at\nBoots. Here is how to get it right, sorted by the person rather than the price tag.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/forget-the-scented-candle-the-fragrance-gift-guide-sorted-by-personality-not-price",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
          }
        },
        "blog_item_h6GKJg": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/The_scent_of_a_British_summer_Thumbnail_jpg.jpg",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "The scent of a British summer: sunshine, sunscreen applied way too late, and a fragrance that somehow captures all of it",
            "excerpt": "The British summer is a rumour that occasionally comes true. You spend 11 months\nyearning for it, and then one morning in June the sky is a colour you haven’t seen in a year\nand the entire country loses its mind. Someone in your office or on the train declares it is\n\"actually too hot now.\" A man three doors down fires up a barbecue with the confidence of a&nbsp;person who has watched precisely one YouTube video. The beer gardens fill by half four.\n\n\nAnd you, having applied sunscreen at 2pm to a shoulder that had already been quietly\nroasting since eleven, are now committed to the day whether your skin likes it or not.\nThere is a smell to all of this, and you know it instantly even if you have never tried to\ndescribe it. Warm tarmac after a brief and pointless shower. Cut grass from a neighbour who\ngot out ahead of the hosepipe ban. Coconut suncream, sharp lager, the particular sweetness\nof strawberries eaten outdoors because eating them indoors felt like a waste of the weather.\nSummer has a scent, and it is doing a lot of emotional work before you have even noticed.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/the-scent-of-a-british-summer-sunshine-sunscreen-applied-way-too-late-and-a-fragrance-that-somehow-captures-all-of-it",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
          }
        },
        "blog_item_TwdbNc": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_13_2026_05_48_11_PM_30e8361b-b087-4e07-84c7-544bc202671d.png",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "Fragrance layering, explained: how to turn two bottles into a signature scent nobody else is wearing",
            "excerpt": "Somewhere in the last couple of years, one bottle of fragrance stopped being enough for anybody. Spend five minutes on TikTok and you will find someone spritzing two at once with the solemn confidence of a Michelin chef, promising a scent no one else in the room could possibly own. It looks like a faff. It looks, frankly, like a plot to make you buy twice as much perfume. It is neither. Layering is one of the oldest tricks in a perfumer's book, finally handed down to the rest of us, and once it clicks you will wonder why you spent years wearing your fragrances one lonely bottle at a time.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/fragrance-layering-explained-how-to-turn-two-bottles-into-a-signature-scent-nobody-else-is-wearing",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
          }
        },
        "blog_item_EAEzxn": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_14_2026_02_16_37_PM_eba35ec2-af98-48d9-92fe-e6908a991071.png",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "Top perfume for men: the gift guide for anyone who has absolutely no idea what to buy the men in their lives",
            "excerpt": "There is a particular breed of man who is impossible to buy for, and you almost certainly live\nwith one, are related to one, or are dating one. Ask him what he wants and he says \"oh,\ndon’t worry about me.\" Left alone he will wear the same aftershave he was given in 2022\nuntil the bottle turns a suspicious yellow. He is never going to replace it himself. That is\nwhere you come in.\nFragrance is the gift most people overlook, mainly because he would never get round to\nbuying it himself. He would use it every day, it is properly personal, and it freshens up a bit of\nhis routine he never thinks about. The only real skill is matching the scent to the man. So\nhere is the shortcut, sorted by the bloke you are really buying for. Each pick is a Scentspired\nbestseller built on high-quality, Swiss-sourced fragrance oil, the bit that makes a scent last\nall day instead of clocking off before lunch.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/top-perfume-for-men-the-gift-guide-for-anyone-who-has-absolutely-no-idea-what-to-buy-the-men-in-their-lives",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
          }
        },
        "blog_item_4WHBAX": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_14_2026_02_16_37_PM_eba35ec2-af98-48d9-92fe-e6908a991071.png",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "The best cologne for men, chosen for you: a gift guide for when \"what do you even want?\" gets you nowhere",
            "excerpt": "Buying a gift for a man can feel like negotiating with someone who refuses to name a ransom.\nYou ask what he wants and get a shrug and a &quot;I really don&#39;t need anything.&quot; He will not send a\nlink, he will not drop a hint, and he will absolutely clock it if a gift card shows up again. Which\nleaves you where you are every year: in a store with a deadline and no plan.\nHere is the case for cologne. He would never spend the money on himself, he will use it every\nmorning, and it refreshes a corner of his routine he stopped thinking about years ago. The only\nreal work is matching the scent to the man instead of grabbing whatever is stacked highest at\nthe counter. So let&#39;s make it easy and go by the guy you are shopping for. Each pick is a\nScentspired bestseller made with high-quality, Swiss-sourced fragrance oil, the thing that keeps\na scent going all day rather than fading out before his second coffee.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/the-best-cologne-for-men-chosen-for-you-a-gift-guide-for-when-quot-what-do-you-even-want-quot-gets-you-nowhere",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
